% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's mixin `as_markers`, compiled by
% psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: the class body
% is lost (docs/simpos/subsystems/window.md §0.3, §1.3, §2.6).  MENDELS
% (IFS No.61), 2026-11-27: a nature of its `graphic` (win_class.esp) and
% of the screen pane (essential_window_with_superior_input_buffer.esp);
% its marker_input makes a 1 x 1 box marker on each (marker.esp:45-56); a
% nature of 7 held programs' classes (window.md §1.3).
%
% THE MANUALS: TM-125 p10 (4.2, 2)) as_markers "the class for suppling
% the function to have markers in the window"; p17 (5.5, 3) markers):
% create_marker/2 `(Window, ^Marker)`, draw_marker/2, erase_marker/2,
% move_marker/4, set_marker_type/3 (box or line), set_marker_size/4,
% get_marker_list/2 "return the list of all markers the window have".
% create_marker/7 `(W, X, Y, Width, Height, Type, ^M)` is MENDELS's form
% (marker.esp:48, 55) and the CESP substitute's (linguist
% with_marker.esp:21-25, window.md §2.6), as standard_io_window.esp's.
% The marker object is marker.esp's (window M8).  Only the making and the
% list are stood in: drawing a marker in an inferior window
% (draw_marker/2, erase_marker/2, move_marker/4) is not, and a send to it
% is refused loudly.

class as_markers has

instance

% OURS representation: the window's markers, in the order made.
attribute markers := [];

% INTERPOLATED (selector and arguments PRINTED-INTERFACE TM-125 p17; body
% OURS): a 16 x 16 box at (0, 0), not drawn (as standard_io_window.esp's).
% LABEL: RECONSTRUCTED-FROM-MANUAL (TM-125 p17 create_marker/2; the size
% OURS)
:create_marker(W, M) :- :create_marker(W, 0, 0, 16, 16, box, M);

% INTERPOLATED (selector and arguments USAGE MENDELS marker.esp:48, see
% the head; body OURS): a marker of Type (box or line, TM-125 p17) at (X,
% Y) of Width x Height, not drawn.
% LABEL: INFERENCE (the arguments from MENDELS and CESP's form; the types
% TM-125 p17)
:create_marker(W, X, Y, Wd, Ht, Type, M) :- marker_type(Type), !,
        :create(#marker, W, X, Y, Wd, Ht, Type, M),
        appended(W!markers, [M], Ms),
        W!markers := Ms;

% INTERPOLATED (selector and arguments PRINTED-INTERFACE TM-125 p17; body
% OURS): the window's markers, in the order made.
% LABEL: RECONSTRUCTED-FROM-MANUAL (TM-125 p17 get_marker_list/2)
:get_marker_list(W, Ms) :- Ms = W!markers;

local

marker_type(box);
marker_type(line);

appended([], L, L);
appended([X | R], L, [X | S]) :- appended(R, L, S);

end.
